---
// One level of the table of contents, and every level below it. Added 2026-09-22, replacing the
// string concatenation that used to live in src/lib/toc.ts and reach the page through set:html.
//
// The recursion is Astro.self (Astro 4, API Reference, "Astro.self"), which lets a component
// render itself. The gain over the string version is not the shape of the code: it is that the
// template escapes the heading text and the href, so the hand-written escapeHtml() the old
// renderList() depended on is gone, and a future edit cannot forget to call it.
//
// The markup is what Hugo's .TableOfContents emits and what the previous version built: nested
// <ul>/<li>, an <a> per heading, and a bare <li> wrapping the next level where a level has no
// heading of its own (a post whose headings start at h2). The id TableOfContents is on the <nav>
// in TableOfContents.astro, not here, because this component renders one list at any depth.
//
// The anchor is written as the raw slug, not percent-encoded, which is what the string version
// produced and what the browser resolves against the heading's id. encodeSlug() from lib/urlize.ts
// is for a path segment in a link to another page; an in-page fragment is not that.
//
// Two differences in the emitted HTML, both checked and both invisible. First, a template keeps
// the whitespace around its expressions, so the built markup reads `<ul> <li> <a ...>` where the
// concatenated string had `<ul><li><a ...>`. Nothing shows it: main.css gives #TableOfContents a
// `display: block` and the lists `list-style: none` with no flex anywhere, so a space between two
// block boxes renders as nothing, and `#TableOfContents > ul > li + li` matches on elements, which
// text nodes do not affect. Second, the <nav> carries a data-astro-cid attribute now, because it
// sits in TableOfContents.astro, which has a scoped style block; the list below does not, since
// this component has no styles of its own. Every rule that targets the table of contents is a
// global id or element selector in main.css, so neither difference reaches the page.
import type { TocNode } from "../lib/toc";

interface Props {
  nodes: TocNode[];
}

const { nodes } = Astro.props;
---

<ul>
  {
    nodes.map((node) => (
      <li>
        {node.heading && (
          <a href={`#${node.heading.slug}`}>{node.heading.text}</a>
        )}
        {node.children.length > 0 && <Astro.self nodes={node.children} />}
      </li>
    ))
  }
</ul>
